From b9d881b51bec33238ccaed8134939c0899d1cd29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alvaro Moran <alvaro.moran@huggingface.co>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:02:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat(model): serve unimplemented archs with the
 Transformers backend

vLLM resolves an architecture that vLLM Neuron has no implementation of
(Granite, Gemma3, Mistral, ...) to vLLM's own GPU model class, which the
Neuron runners cannot run. Add registry.resolve_model_cls(), used by both
model runners: when the resolved class is not a Neuron model, serve the
decoder model with the Transformers backend, as upstream vLLM does with
model_impl="auto" for the architectures it has no implementation of. The
transformers class must support custom attention functions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
